<title>UK: World drug sales advanced in Jan-Sept -IMS.</title>
<headline>World drug sales advanced in Jan-Sept -IMS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmaceutical sales in 10 of the world's top markets rose six percent year-on-year in local currency terms in January to September, market researcher IMS International said.</p>
<p>IMS detailed retail pharmacy sales as follows, in billion dollars. Growth rates in local currency terms -</p>
<p>		    Jan-Sept 96     Jan-Sept 95     Percent growth</p>
<p> U.S.		  43.3		40.4		 7.0</p>
<p> Canada		 2.8		 2.6		 4.0</p>
<p> Germany	     12.6		12.3		 8.0</p>
<p> France		10.9		10.8		 2.0</p>
<p> Italy		  6.6		 5.6		11.0</p>
<p> UK		     4.9		 4.6		10.0</p>
<p> Spain		  3.8		 3.5		10.0</p>
<p> Netherlands	  1.5		 1.5		 1.0</p>
<p> Belgium		1.5		 1.5		 7.0</p>
<p> Japan		 17.2		 19.9		2.0</p>
<p> Selected world   105.1		102.7		6.0</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
